WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.549 --> 00:00:05.930
Establishing a mood from the get-go is monumentally
important for a movie, especially for films

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:07.580
of the horror-thriller genre.

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:11.940
A movie's first few scenes can either strike
an audience with terror, or signal yawns to

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:16.059
come … which is particularly scary for horror
fans.

00:00:16.059 --> 00:00:20.269
In the case of these freaky flicks, the first
ten minutes are terrifying for all the right

00:00:20.269 --> 00:00:21.269
reasons.

00:00:21.269 --> 00:00:22.999
A Nightmare on Elm Street

00:00:22.999 --> 00:00:28.109
The opening credits for Wes Craven's A Nightmare
on Elm Street introduce Freddie Krueger without

00:00:28.109 --> 00:00:32.829
showing his burn-damaged face, as he puts
together his terrifying claw in his boiler

00:00:32.829 --> 00:00:33.829
room.

00:00:33.829 --> 00:00:36.210
Once his blades are ready, we meet victim
number one.

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:40.780
Tina is a pajama-clad blonde who finds herself
running down the halls of his leaky lair,

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:45.089
all while Krueger cackles at the uselessness
of her escape attempt.

00:00:45.089 --> 00:00:48.840
Just as she's about to eat it at the hands
of his new weapon, she awakens to realize

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:50.760
it's all just a dream.

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:55.429
Judging by the slash marks on her gown, though,
we already know in the film's first few moments

00:00:55.429 --> 00:00:58.820
that it's much worse than some normal nightmare.

00:00:58.820 --> 00:00:59.820
Scream

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:04.860
The opening scene from Scream was an instant
horror favorite, and for good reason.

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:09.470
Casey Becker is your everyday teen girl, cooking
up some popcorn in her home alone, while her

00:01:09.470 --> 00:01:10.940
parents are out on a date.

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:14.800
She gets a call from an apparent prankster
who wants to talk about scary movies, and

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:17.830
Casey thinks it's all just fun and games and
plays along…

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:19.540
"Do you like scary movies?"

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:20.540
"Uh huh."

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:23.220
But then the conversation starts to turn dark.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:27.740
She quickly begins to realize this isn't a
joke, especially once the caller reveals he's

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:30.860
abducted her boyfriend, Steve, and bound him
on her back deck.

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:34.890
Her fight-or-flight response kicks in, but
the latter option isn't available because

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:38.800
the masked boogeyman has gone from lurking
outside to inside.

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:42.470
The villain's speed and ability to predict
her every move, courtesy of the house's open

00:01:42.470 --> 00:01:45.100
window scheme, is absolutely crippling.

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:49.170
Making things worse, when the killer finally
strikes, Casey's parents have come back home,

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:51.820
but she can't scream loud enough for anyone
to help her.

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:53.520
"Mom!"

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:56.860
Now, who hasn't had that nightmare before?

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:57.920
Jaws

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:03.360
All Chrissi wanted to do was take a little
night swim with the cute guy she met at a

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:04.360
party.

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:08.750
While she's practically a fish in the moonlit
water, the dude isn't so convinced he's capable

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:09.750
of swimming.

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:12.860
He's pretty drunk, after all, so Chrissie
goes it alone…and gets about halfway to

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:15.890
a buoy before that ominous cello music kicks
in.

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:20.580
Chrissie is all smiles in the dark until something
starts to pull her under.

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:24.780
She's left thrashing and begging for help,
but her wannabe boyfriend is unaware on the

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:25.780
beach.

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:29.280
Desperate, she tries to cling to the buoy,
but she knows she's done for.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:31.580
"Oh my God, I'm gonna die!"

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:34.460
The shark drags her down and makes a meal
of the poor girl.

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:39.230
Meanwhile, Mr. Helpful is still over there,
drunkenly murmuring to himself on the sand.

00:02:39.230 --> 00:02:40.890
Talk about a beach bum.

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:43.069
The Ring

00:02:43.069 --> 00:02:47.050
When we first meet Katie and Becca, they're
blabbering about the woes of modern tech,

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:50.000
but one of them is harboring a very dark secret.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:54.140
It's not the "electrorays" that pose a threat
to the girls -- it's the fabled video tape

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:58.040
Katie has watched that's said to kill anyone
who watches it a week later.

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:02.310
Somehow, she's not bothered by the ominous
warning label that was attached to the tape

00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:06.700
or the fact that she received a frightening
phone call soon after her screening of it.

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:09.910
She even fake chokes to show just how unscared
she is.

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:13.660
But her playfulness comes to a halt once things
around the house start turning themselves

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:16.730
on and off and everything's soaking wet all
of a sudden.

00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:20.750
When she goes to find Becca, she discovers
the video is playing in her room, and she

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:23.310
gasps as her face turns to stone.

00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:28.920
If you've been hesitant to chuck that old
VCR, well, this might change your mind.

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:30.360
Final Destination

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:35.130
The first scene in Final Destination set the
shock value bar pretty high for the films

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:36.130
to follow.

00:03:36.130 --> 00:03:39.860
In the beginning, we meet Alex, a high school
student who's boarding Flight 180 with his

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:40.860
school pals.

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:44.700
They're excited for their field trip to Paris,
until all hell breaks loose and the plane

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:49.301
starts to fall apart mid-air, killing some
of the passengers in grisly ways before it

00:03:49.301 --> 00:03:50.960
explodes and takes the rest.

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:56.190
Then all of a sudden, Alex wakes up in a cold
sweat and realizes it was just a dream.

00:03:56.190 --> 00:03:59.900
He's convinced this is some kind of premonition
that everyone needs to heed.

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:03.590
But after screaming his warnings to the rest
of the passengers, Alex is booted from the

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:06.200
plane, along with a few unhappy tagalongs.

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:10.319
The group is also made to wait in the airport
as the plane takes off for the excursion of

00:04:10.319 --> 00:04:15.000
a lifetime, but then Alex's vision comes true
as the plane blows up.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:18.729
After the first film, the sequels tried to
follow that explosive formula, with a massive

00:04:18.729 --> 00:04:23.840
highway pile-up, a roller coaster ride gone
wrong, a race car demolition derby, and a

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:25.319
devastating bridge collapse.

00:04:25.319 --> 00:04:29.979
So, if you want to see some movies that are
frontloaded with massive intensity, the Final

00:04:29.979 --> 00:04:34.379
Destination movies are your, well, final destination.

00:04:34.379 --> 00:04:35.900
Night of the Living Dead

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:40.810
In the introduction to George Romero's seminal
zombie flick, we meet Johnny and Barbra, a

00:04:40.810 --> 00:04:44.779
pair of siblings who've trekked out to put
a wreath on their dad's grave.

00:04:44.779 --> 00:04:48.830
Due to technical problems with their radio,
they don't hear the warning that's being broadcast

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:51.830
about what they're about to encounter in the
cemetery.

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:56.080
While Barb's paying her respects, Johnny notices
a weird man walking through the graveyard

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:57.559
and makes light of the arrival.

00:04:57.559 --> 00:04:59.909
"They're coming for you, Barbara."

00:04:59.909 --> 00:05:04.499
Little does he know, his joke has just set
the tone for everything that's about to happen.

00:05:04.499 --> 00:05:08.529
Barb tries to pass the stranger, but he reaches
out and grabs her, so Johnny jumps to his

00:05:08.529 --> 00:05:12.770
sister's defense, but he's knocked out cold
while trying to wrestle the man to the ground.

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:16.800
Terrified, Barbra kicks off her shoes and
runs away to lock herself inside her car.

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:20.669
The walker doesn't suffer windows, though,
so Barbra releases the parking brake, hoping

00:05:20.669 --> 00:05:22.340
she can roll away to safety.

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:25.270
But a tree stops her progress, forcing her
to flee on foot.

00:05:25.270 --> 00:05:29.569
When she enters an abandoned farmhouse that
seems relatively safe, it's only the beginning

00:05:29.569 --> 00:05:33.800
of her bout with this deadly humanoid thing…and
many others to come.

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:34.800
Thanks for watching!

